    "2d98e13d": {
      "text": "Two friends want to grow a lotus for a science report. They plant a seed and look after it.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-02.mp3",
      "start": 7.2413,
      "duration": 5.2267,
      "speed": 0.94,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "0bfb7d8a": {
      "text": "Later, they find a surprising plant. Its leaves catch a small insect. They have mixed up the seeds!",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-02.mp3",
      "start": 12.818,
      "duration": 5.9733,
      "speed": 0.94,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "ba4f5eaf": {
      "text": "It has big leaves.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-02.mp3",
      "start": 19.1413,
      "duration": 1.3013,
      "speed": 0.92,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "033a7856": {
      "text": "How lovely!",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-02.mp3",
      "start": 20.7927,
      "duration": 1.0027,
      "speed": 0.92,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "91d13838": {
      "text": "A tomato plant has roots, a stem and leaves. It can also have flowers and fruit. Each part has a different job.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-02.mp3",
      "start": 22.1453,
      "duration": 7.2107,
      "speed": 0.94,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "9d053e90": {
      "text": "Under the soil, the roots hold the plant steady. They take in water and minerals.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-02.mp3",
      "start": 29.706,
      "duration": 4.6293,
      "speed": 0.94,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "49bfd63b": {
      "text": "Water travels up through the stem to the leaves. The leaves use sunlight to help make food for the plant.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-02.mp3",
      "start": 34.6853,
      "duration": 5.6747,
      "speed": 0.94,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "14f5105e": {
      "text": "Flowers can develop into fruit with seeds inside. When seeds reach suitable soil and conditions, new plants can grow.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-02.mp3",
      "start": 40.71,
      "duration": 7.3813,
      "speed": 0.94,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "9e0d0e96": {
      "text": "The stem carries water to the leaves.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-02.mp3",
      "start": 48.4413,
      "duration": 2.0907,
      "speed": 0.92,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "a78e53a2": {
      "text": "At the botanical gardens, the children notice an unusual tulip. Its flower reminds them of an ice cream cone.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-02.mp3",
      "start": 50.882,
      "duration": 7.2533,
      "speed": 0.94,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "e9e2f02f": {
      "text": "Nearby, a meat-eating plant has special leaves. They look like small mouths. The plant can catch insects.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-03.mp3",
      "start": 0.0,
      "duration": 6.4,
      "speed": 0.94,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "eae84db5": {
      "text": "Creepers spread across a wall. In the pond, broad water-lily leaves remind the children of green umbrellas.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-03.mp3",
      "start": 6.75,
      "duration": 6.8267,
      "speed": 0.94,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "972f5c57": {
      "text": "The water-lily flowers rise above the muddy water. The children are surprised by their clean, beautiful petals.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-03.mp3",
      "start": 13.9267,
      "duration": 7.104,
      "speed": 0.94,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "586288a3": {
      "text": "This leaf looks like a fan.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-03.mp3",
      "start": 21.3807,
      "duration": 1.664,
      "speed": 0.92,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "2ce6793f": {
      "text": "The tulips are beautiful.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-03.mp3",
      "start": 23.3947,
      "duration": 1.5573,
      "speed": 0.92,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "1f6a4415": {
      "text": "The reading asks whether plants can give us clues about the weather. It describes four-o’clock flowers, pine cones and morning glories.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-03.mp3",
      "start": 25.302,
      "duration": 7.8507,
      "speed": 0.94,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "d58f4584": {
      "text": "In the reading, four-o’clock flowers that close early are linked with a sunny day. Flowers still open after six are linked with clouds or rain.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-03.mp3",
      "start": 33.5027,
      "duration": 9.1733,
      "speed": 0.94,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "4e57f03e": {
      "text": "Pine-cone scales open in dry conditions and close when they become wet. This movement helps protect the seeds.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-03.mp3",
      "start": 43.026,
      "duration": 7.0187,
      "speed": 0.94,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "6b311efd": {
      "text": "We can use if to plan for tomorrow: if it rains, we will take an umbrella. We observe plants, but also check a weather forecast.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-03.mp3",
      "start": 50.3947,
      "duration": 8.0427,
      "speed": 0.94,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "c17f2508": {
      "text": "Can roots take in water? Yes, they can.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-03.mp3",
      "start": 58.7873,
      "duration": 2.496,
      "speed": 0.92,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "0c73c3e8": {
      "text": "The scales close when the pine cone is wet.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-03.mp3",
      "start": 61.6333,
      "duration": 2.432,
      "speed": 0.92,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "b94caa64": {
      "text": "If it rains tomorrow, we will take an umbrella.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-03.mp3",
      "start": 64.4153,
      "duration": 2.7307,
      "speed": 0.92,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "11a3553d": {
      "text": "Start a plant poster with the name. Then describe what you can see: the stem, leaves and flower.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-03.mp3",
      "start": 67.496,
      "duration": 5.9093,
      "speed": 0.94,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "c859d501": {
      "text": "For example, a sunflower has a tall stem and a large yellow flower. Its flower looks like the sun.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-03.mp3",
      "start": 73.7553,
      "duration": 6.336,
      "speed": 0.94,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "02e2d9af": {
      "text": "Add one interesting detail and a picture. Check the facts before you present your poster to a friend.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-03.mp3",
      "start": 80.4413,
      "duration": 6.2293,
      "speed": 0.94,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "3d3f72f3": {
      "text": "An observation notebook keeps what we see separate from what we guess. We can record a pine cone, the time and whether it is wet or dry.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-03.mp3",
      "start": 87.0207,
      "duration": 8.4907,
      "speed": 0.94,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "736e2a27": {
      "text": "We compare observations on different days. One observation is a clue, but it does not prove every weather prediction.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-04.mp3",
      "start": 0.0,
      "duration": 7.3173,
      "speed": 0.94,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
