      "file": "unit3-05.mp3",
      "start": 14.538,
      "duration": 6.336,
      "speed": 0.94,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "5430404b": {
      "text": "An elephant points out the mistake. The panda’s hometown is in China. The friends need the right information before they keep going.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-05.mp3",
      "start": 21.224,
      "duration": 8.2773,
      "speed": 0.94,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "afe65fa3": {
      "text": "We are from China.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-05.mp3",
      "start": 29.8513,
      "duration": 1.2587,
      "speed": 0.92,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "8cfaf792": {
      "text": "The chant introduces pandas from Sichuan. They are black and white, and the chant compares their rolling bodies to a ball.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-05.mp3",
      "start": 31.46,
      "duration": 7.4027,
      "speed": 0.94,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "bc2ed52e": {
      "text": "Next come monkeys from Guizhou. In the chant, they are yellow and brown and jump among the trees.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-05.mp3",
      "start": 39.2127,
      "duration": 5.7173,
      "speed": 0.94,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "10043428": {
      "text": "The elephants in the chant come from Yunnan. Their bodies are light grey. They use their trunks to spray water over themselves.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-06.mp3",
      "start": 0.0,
      "duration": 7.4453,
      "speed": 0.94,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "8f6a3726": {
      "text": "These pandas live in Sichuan. They eat bamboo.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-06.mp3",
      "start": 7.7953,
      "duration": 2.9227,
      "speed": 0.92,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "0f5311f7": {
      "text": "Shenshen watches a programme with her mum. They see a family of elephants playing in a river in Yunnan.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-06.mp3",
      "start": 11.068,
      "duration": 5.76,
      "speed": 0.94,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "b7932e4c": {
      "text": "Mum explains that elephants also live in India and Africa. Places with trees and water are important to them.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-06.mp3",
      "start": 17.178,
      "duration": 7.104,
      "speed": 0.94,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "38825f19": {
      "text": "A baby elephant swims away. Its mother pulls it back by the tail. The programme also shows a farmer giving the elephants bananas.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-06.mp3",
      "start": 24.632,
      "duration": 8.32,
      "speed": 0.94,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "115fd40b": {
      "text": "The elephant is swimming.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-06.mp3",
      "start": 33.302,
      "duration": 1.536,
      "speed": 0.92,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "8f3e54ee": {
      "text": "How cute!",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-06.mp3",
      "start": 35.188,
      "duration": 0.9813,
      "speed": 0.92,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "7689863f": {
      "text": "Polar bears live in the Arctic near the North Pole. Their thick fur helps them keep warm, and their coats look white against the ice and snow.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-06.mp3",
      "start": 36.5193,
      "duration": 8.3627,
      "speed": 0.94,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "4cccc0e5": {
      "text": "They are strong swimmers. The reading describes them catching seals and fish for food and resting on snow.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-06.mp3",
      "start": 45.232,
      "duration": 6.208,
      "speed": 0.94,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "2742d3ae": {
      "text": "As the climate warms, sea ice melts. Losing sea ice makes life harder for polar bears because they use it to reach their prey.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-06.mp3",
      "start": 51.79,
      "duration": 8.1067,
      "speed": 0.94,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "defe6d33": {
      "text": "We can learn about their homes and explain why sea ice matters. A clear explanation connects a change with its effect.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-06.mp3",
      "start": 60.2467,
      "duration": 7.2533,
      "speed": 0.94,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "d6c33031": {
      "text": "The ice is melting because the weather is getting warmer.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-06.mp3",
      "start": 67.85,
      "duration": 3.3707,
      "speed": 0.92,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "7ed58b20": {
      "text": "There is lots of ice.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-06.mp3",
      "start": 71.5707,
      "duration": 1.3653,
      "speed": 0.92,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "7be070a5": {
      "text": "Choose an animal and collect four kinds of information: its home, food, appearance and abilities. Add a picture that matches your words.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-06.mp3",
      "start": 73.286,
      "duration": 8.5973,
      "speed": 0.94,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "721f5dde": {
      "text": "For the monkeys in the example, the home is Guizhou. They eat fruit and leaves, have long tails and arms, and can climb trees and swing on branches.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-06.mp3",
      "start": 82.2333,
      "duration": 9.2587,
      "speed": 0.94,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "575e1f19": {
      "text": "Finish by describing one action in the picture. Say what the animal is doing now, then check that every sentence matches the picture.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-06.mp3",
      "start": 91.842,
      "duration": 8.1707,
      "speed": 0.94,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "27a4bfc4": {
      "text": "The extra reading visits different animal homes. A panda eats bamboo in a Chinese forest, while monkeys move through warm woodland.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-07.mp3",
      "start": 0.0,
      "duration": 8.384,
      "speed": 0.94,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    },
    "f33f8b1d": {
      "text": "It also describes a mother elephant caring for her calf and polar bears living in the Arctic. Protecting animals includes caring for the places they need.",
      "lang": "en",
      "file": "unit3-07.mp3",
      "start": 8.734,
      "duration": 10.0053,
      "speed": 0.94,
      "listened": false,
      "contentReview": "pending"
    }
  },
